# ============================================================================
# What does NOT need to be sent to EAS to build the app.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# The project tarball had grown to 108 MB, and uploading it over the
# connection these builds are started from failed repeatedly — once at
# 97.6 MB of 108, with an EPIPE, after six minutes. Most of that payload was
# marketing artwork and screenshots: material that has nothing to do with
# compiling an Android binary and that is re-uploaded in full on every build.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING
#
# EAS uses this file INSTEAD OF .gitignore, not in addition to it. Every rule
# that protects the upload has to be restated here — and the one that matters
# most is `android/`, which holds a local prebuild with Gradle output and is
# over three gigabytes. Leaving it out of this file would not make the upload
# slightly larger; it would make it impossible.
#
# The rule of thumb: if the Gradle build cannot read it, it does not belong in
# the tarball.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Dependencies and build output (restated from .gitignore) --------------
node_modules/
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.turbo/
.expo/
.expo-shared/
web-build/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
*.lcov
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ---- Native projects: EAS runs its own prebuild ----------------------------
# android/ alone is >3 GB of local Gradle output on a working checkout.
apps/seamflow-app/android/
apps/seamflow-app/ios/
apps/seamflow-client/android/
apps/seamflow-client/ios/

# ---- Secrets and signing material ------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision

# ---- Version control, logs, editors, OS ------------------------------------
.git/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Previously-built binaries ---------------------------------------------
*.apk
*.aab
backups/

# ---- Everything below is the actual saving ---------------------------------
# Artwork, store listings, screenshots and written documentation. None of it
# is read by the build, and together it was most of the upload.
docs/
play-ready-screenshots/
play-ready-tablet/
phone screenshots. /
logos-png/
logos-svg/
new logo/
Claude outputs/
shots 4 appstore/
tab shots 4 appstore/
README.txt

# Code kept only for reference — the app does not import it.
apps/seamflow-app/app-legacy/
apps/seamflow-app/src-legacy/
apps/seamflow-app/app-example/

# Supabase CLI scratch space.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# Tooling state for this repo's assistants — transcripts, caches and settings.
# Seventeen megabytes of it, and not one byte is read by Gradle.
.claude/

# iOS signing: never upload the local credentials map.
credentials.json
